# SQL's `count(*)`: DS0117 with a fix to `count()`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | summarize n = count(*) by customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..57
  PIPELINE@0..56
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    SUMMARIZE_OP@20..56
      IDENT@20..29 "summarize"
      WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@30..42
        NAME@30..31
          IDENT@30..31 "n"
        WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
        EQ@32..33 "="
        WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
        CALL_EXPR@34..42
          NAME_REF@34..39
            IDENT@34..39 "count"
          ARG_LIST@39..42
            L_PAREN@39..40 "("
            ERROR@40..41
              STAR@40..41 "*"
            R_PAREN@41..42 ")"
      WHITESPACE@42..43 " "
      BY_CLAUSE@43..56
        IDENT@43..45 "by"
        WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
        NAMED_EXPR@46..56
          NAME_REF@46..56
            IDENT@46..56 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@56..57 "\n"

error[DS0117]: `count(*)` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:41
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | summarize n = count(*) by customerId
  |                                         ^ `count()` counts rows without a `*`
  |
  = help: write `count()`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | summarize n = count() by customerId
which parses without errors
